  "_about": "Priors for how prices move around Black Friday, by category. They are rough approximations of the patterns reported for recent US holiday seasons (Adobe Digital Economy Index holiday reports and price-tracker write-ups): discounts build through November, peak from Thanksgiving to Cyber Monday, then fade the week after, with a smaller second dip in mid-December. Edit these numbers freely. 'curve' maps days from Black Friday (0 = Black Friday, 3 = Cyber Monday) to discount intensity, where 1.0 is the deepest point of the season; values between keys are interpolated. 'everyday_discount' is the usual street discount off list price/MSRP outside sales; 'peak_extra_discount' is the extra drop off that street price at the peak.",
